I had a couple ideas about character classes:

1. "Magician." In some mythological traditions, the primary power of a
wizard is the ability to shapeshift... have this guy start out with 
intrinsic polymorph, and intrinsic polymorph control, and _nothing else_.

Maybe have "Wizard" moved to "Magic user" and make the Wizard the
shapeshifting character...

2. Sidhe. Starts out with oodles of hit points, bronze plate mail,
silver sabre, bow, arrows of slaying... sound powerful? Well, there's
this one teensy problem they seem to have with iron. Can't wield it,
can't wear it, plus in addition to up to twice normal damage (this should
be random) it should also randomly stun, confuse, and make deathly sick.

Of course, tradition seems to be divided as to whether or not Sidhe could
stand iron, depending on how much germanic influence there was on the
tradition...

